{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the equation \\(\\frac{6r^2 - 19r - 7}{2r-7} = 4r-3\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Eliminate the denominator by multiplying both sides by \\(2r-7\\):**\n   \\[\n   6r^2 - 19r - 7 = (4r - 3)(2r - 7)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Expand the right-hand side:**\n   \\[\n   (4r - 3)(2r - 7) = 4r \\cdot 2r + 4r \\cdot (-7) + (-3) \\cdot 2r + (-3) \\cdot (-7)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 8r^2 - 28r - 6r + 21\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 8r^2 - 34r + 21\n   \\]\n\n3. **Set the expanded form equal to the left-hand side:**\n   \\[\n   6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 34r + 21\n   \\]\n\n4. **Move all terms to one side to form a quadratic equation:**\n   \\[\n   6r^2 - 19r - 7 - 8r^2 + 34r - 21 = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   -2r^2 + 15r - 28 = 0\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply the entire equation by \\(-1\\) to simplify:**\n   \\[\n   2r^2 - 15r + 28 = 0\n   \\]\n\n6. **Solve the quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\(r = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = 2\\), \\(b = -15\\), and \\(c = 28\\):**\n   \\[\n   r = \\frac{-(-15) \\pm \\sqrt{(-15)^2 - 4 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 28}}{2 \\cdot 2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   r = \\frac{15 \\pm \\sqrt{225 - 224}}{4}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   r = \\frac{15 \\pm \\sqrt{1}}{4}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   r = \\frac{15 \\pm 1}{4}\n   \\]\n\n","prefix_end":1146,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,23606,1124,11520,37018,90,21,81,61,17,481,220,16,24,81,481,220,22,15170,17,81,12,22,92,284,220,19,81,12,18,59,701,582,686,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,41013,3277,279,46912,553,84192,2176,11067,553,17767,17,81,12,22,59,1648,1019,256,1124,9640,256,220,21,81,61,17,481,220,16,24,81,481,220,22,284,320,19,81,481,220,18,2376,17,81,481,220,22,340,256,1124,2533,17,13,3070,38946,279,1290,24413,3108,25,1019,256,1124,9640,256,320,19,81,481,220,18,2376,17,81,481,220,22,8,284,220,19,81,1124,50853,220,17,81,488,220,19,81,112